> I asked this question some years ago, though specifically for pets, and
> didn't get anything more useful as answer than the best trick I already
> knew - for those monster types valid, provoke a his/her message.
>
> Do all monsters have genders (in the code)? Mimics, piercers, yellow
> lights, etc?

   No, many monsters have M2_NEUTER, which means they're just "it".
In addition, all player-visible messages go via the mhim() macro,
which calls pronoun_gender(), which causes "him" and "her" to be used
only for monsters which are non-neuter, visible, and at least one of

   (1) humanoid,
   (2) unique (Oracle, high priests of Foo), or
   (3) named with the M2_PNAME flag (Medusa, Croesus, Juiblex,...)

   I don't know how to discover the gender of a monster in-game,
either, but I agree it ought to be possible somehow, just for
the sake of realism.

